the license of a tired toaster

you may use this thing.
you may copy this thing.
you may modify this thing.
you may show this thing to your friends.
your friends may wonder why this thing exists.

you may not blame the toaster.
you may not blame the author for your questionable folder choices.
you may not ask despair to fix your broken code.
it is not a therapist.

if the program deletes files, it is doing the only thing it knows.
if it does not delete files, it is probably having a bad day.

this license is not a standard open source license.
it is mostly a piece of paper having an existential crisis.

no warranty. no promises. no emotional support.
